# runstate: repository rules

## What this is

runstate is a stateful agent orchestration runtime. The unit of work is the
**run**: budgeted, resumable, receipted. Three builder workspaces assemble
into one `runstate` package:

- `runtime/` -> `runstate.runtime`: the Run model, Budget/Usage, SQLite
  ledger, provider router (`get_provider`). Owns ALL state. Depends on
  nothing product-level.
- `integrations/` -> `runstate.protocol`: the MCP server
  (`runstate.protocol.server`) plus sponsor adapters (`zetaris.py`,
  `meterless.py`). Depends on runtime only.
- `surface/` -> `runstate.cli`, `runstate.runner`, packaging, docs, tests.
  Depends on runtime and protocol. Nothing imports the CLI.

The dependency rule is one-directional: surface -> protocol -> runtime.
Never invert it.

## Conventions

- Public API lives in `runstate.runtime`: `create_run`, `get_run`,
  `cancel_run`, `list_runs`, `get_provider`, `Budget`, `RunNotFound`,
  `append_step`, `get_steps`, `check_budget`, `cost_for_usage`. Import from
  these stable paths; do not reach into private modules.
- The run id attribute is `run.run_id` (not `run.id`). Statuses: `pending`,
  `running`, `success`, `unverified`, `exhausted`, `failed`, `cancelled`.
- Runs have NO `outcome` attribute. Outcomes are ledger steps with
  `kind="outcome"`; read them via `get_steps(run_id)`.
- The runner loop (`runstate.runner.drive_run`) is the ONLY executor. The
  model signals completion with a `FINAL:`-prefixed message. Budgets are
  checked before every step via `check_budget`; the run is saved after every
  step so crashes are resumable.
- Ledger location is `RUNSTATE_DB_PATH` (default `~/.runstate/ledger.db`).
  Tests MUST isolate it per test (see `tests/conftest.py` pattern).
- CLI and runner import the runtime LAZILY so `runstate doctor` reports a
  missing runtime as a checklist failure, never a traceback.
- `runstate doctor`: missing provider and missing MCP server are `[warn]`,
  never `[FAIL]`. Only `runstate run` requires a provider.
- Provider config is env-only: `RUNSTATE_PROVIDER=nebius|openai` plus
  `NEBIUS_API_KEY`/`OPENAI_API_KEY`. Never fall back to another provider
  silently; never persist keys.

## Quality bar

No stubs, no TODOs in shipped code. Every doc command must actually run
(verify before writing). Full suite: `python -m pytest` from `surface/`,
all green. New behavior must be reachable via the CLI, the MCP server, or
documented in README/QUICKSTART/ARCHITECTURE.

## Writing

Never use em dashes in any writing. Prefer plain ASCII in docs and CLI
output.
